𒑰 DUB.SAR 1.0 Example: Exact Sexagesimal Arithmetic
𒑰 Difficulty: Beginner
𒑰 Concept: Exact Sexagesimal Arithmetic & Fractions
𒑰 Mode: Mixed (Cuneiform syntax with Latin identifiers)
𒑰
𒑰 Purpose:
𒑰   Demonstrates exact rational arithmetic using positional sexagesimal fractions
𒑰   and rational numbers, eliminating floating-point rounding drift.
𒑰
𒑰 Expected Output:
𒑰   Sum (0;30 + 0;20):
𒑰   0;50
𒑰   Difference (1 - 0;15):
𒑰   0;45
𒑰   Product (0;30 * 0;20):
𒑰   0;10
𒑰   Division (1 / 0;20):
𒑰   3

𒂊𒁹
    half : 0;30
    third : 0;20
    quarter : 0;15
    one : 1

    sum_val :
        half
        third
        𒍣

    diff_val :
        one
        quarter
        𒋫

    prod_val :
        half
        third
        𒊭

    div_val :
        one
        third
        𒉌

𒅗𒁹
    𒁹𒀀 "Sum (0;30 + 0;20):"
    𒁹𒀀 sum_val
    𒁹𒀀 "Difference (1 - 0;15):"
    𒁹𒀀 diff_val
    𒁹𒀀 "Product (0;30 * 0;20):"
    𒁹𒀀 prod_val
    𒁹𒀀 "Division (1 / 0;20):"
    𒁹𒀀 div_val
